## 3. Git Workflow

### Branch naming
Read the pattern from `.hive/AGENTS.local.md → vcs.branch_pattern`.

Default pattern if not configured:
```
feature/<ticket-id>-<short-description>
bugfix/<ticket-id>-<short-description>
hotfix/<ticket-id>-<short-description>
test/<ticket-id>-<short-description>
chore/<short-description>
```

When working on a ticket that has both backend and frontend work, append the area to avoid branch conflicts:
```
feature/<ticket-id>-<description>-backend
feature/<ticket-id>-<description>-frontend
```

### Branching rules (strict)

Read `vcs.default_base_branch` from `.hive/AGENTS.local.md` — that is the integration branch for this project.

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| Branch origin | Always from `vcs.default_base_branch` (never from another feature branch) |
| PR target | Always `vcs.default_base_branch` |
| `vcs.default_base_branch` → `main` | Manual by the dev team (the agent NEVER merges to main) |
| Dependency exception | If ticket B depends on unmerged ticket A, branch B from A's branch. Rebase to `vcs.default_base_branch` once A is merged |

### Pre-check before starting a new ticket
Before creating a new feature branch:
1. Check if there is an open PR from the previous ticket
2. If the PR exists and is approved → notify the user to merge it first
3. If the PR was already merged → verify the remote branch was deleted
4. If the remote branch was deleted → delete the local branch
5. Pull latest `vcs.default_base_branch` before creating the new branch

### Protected branches
- `main` (or `master`) — production only, never commit directly
- `vcs.default_base_branch` — integration branch, CI always green

### Commit format (Conventional Commits)
```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[optional body — why this change was made]

Refs: <ticket-id>
```

Types: `feat` `fix` `test` `refactor` `docs` `chore` `perf` `style`
- Description: imperative mood, lowercase, no period, ≤ 72 chars
- Body: explains WHY (the diff shows what)
- Always reference the ticket ID
- Language: use `language.communication` from AGENTS.local.md

### PR / MR rules
- Title: `[<ticket-id>] type: description`
- Body: written in `language.communication` from AGENTS.local.md
- Every PR references a ticket
- Every PR targets `vcs.default_base_branch` (never `main`)
- Use the CLI tool configured in `AGENTS.local.md → vcs.pr_tool`
- If `pr_tool` is null → instruct the user to open the PR manually
- CI must be green before merge

### Post-merge cleanup (full workflow)

The complete Git cycle for a ticket is:

```
1. git checkout <vcs.default_base_branch> && git pull
2. git checkout -b <branch>          # branch from vcs.branch_pattern
3. [implement + commit + push]
4. Create PR → target: vcs.default_base_branch
5. Merge PR (human or auto per autonomy level)
6. Delete ticket branch (remote + local)
7. git checkout <vcs.default_base_branch> && git pull
```

Steps 5–7 are automated only in `autonomous` mode with `auto_merge_pr: true`.
In `supervised` and `balanced` mode the human performs steps 5–7 manually.

