## Event Logging — events.jsonl

All agents write to `.hive/events.jsonl` (append-only, one JSON object per line).

### Schema

Every event must include these base fields:

```jsonl
{
  "ts": "<ISO-8601 timestamp>",
  "cmd": "<command that triggered this: /ship | /enrich | /plan-be | etc>",
  "ticket": "<ticket ID or null>",
  "stage": "<stage name: enrich | plan-be | tdd | dev-be | commit | etc>",
  "status": "<complete | failed | started | checkpoint>",
  "duration_s": <seconds as number, or null if not applicable>
}
```

### Extended fields (add when relevant)

```jsonl
{
  "tokens": <token count for this stage>,
  "event": "<action | decision | file_created | file_modified | test_run | commit | pr_created>",
  "detail": "<human-readable description of what happened>",
  "error": "<error message if status=failed>"
}
```

### Rules
- **Append-only** — never modify existing lines
- **One event per line** — valid JSON, no multi-line
- **Always write on stage complete AND stage start**
- **In autonomous mode**: write an event for every significant action (see orchestrator.md)
- **Tracked in git** — the whole team shares this file; it is the shared activity log of the project
- **Schema is stable** — adding fields is allowed; removing or renaming existing fields is a breaking change

