## Anti-Patterns

These patterns are **never acceptable**. The AI MUST reject, refactor, or flag them when encountered.

| Pattern | Why | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Business logic in transport layer (controller/handler/route) | Violates SRP; untestable without HTTP | Move to use case / application service |
| Direct cross-domain data access (Service A queries Service B's DB) | Breaks DDD bounded context isolation | Expose a domain event or API contract |
| Hardcoded environment values in source code | Config leaks; breaks multi-env | Read from env vars; fail fast on startup |
| Skipping the failing test before implementation | Defeats TDD purpose; no coverage guarantee | Write failing test first, then implement |
| `TODO` / `FIXME` committed to production paths | Tech debt that compounds | Either fix now or create a ticket |
| Catching all exceptions silently (`except: pass`, `catch {}`) | Swallows real errors; invisible failures | Log with context, rethrow or map to domain error |
| Magic numbers or strings inline | Unreadable; change in one place breaks others | Named constant or config value |
